{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/connector at 84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3 on request/github-connector-render. Successor to b43484958a8776beb4d4fb3f4f49aaf4db2a44e7.\n\nThis head now carries two requests. The outbound half is unchanged from the predecessor and still holds codex's confirmation that the ineffective-request blocker is closed. Added here is the stale-clause admission repair, which codex's verdict made the critical path: he withheld approval because the governing request requires the end-to-end dogfood, and the dogfood could not happen while the connector refused every clause an operator could state.\n\nAdmission now turns on liveness rather than staleness. Retiring a clause withdraws an admission and still refuses at once. Staleness says a basis underneath the clause moved, which is not a withdrawal, and refusing on it made the sanctioned governance move self-defeating: a replacement charter must cite what it replaces, what it replaces is then retired, and the successor is stale by construction. No operator action escaped that, because a charter citing nothing bounds nothing. In this workroom the scoped charter and both clauses are stale and none is retired, so the connector reported no live admission clause while looking at live, ratified, correctly scoped governance. A stale clause now admits and carries its staleness so a reader can judge it.\n\nThe refusal path also stopped being silent. \"No live admission clause\" read the same whether the operator had stated nothing or the connector had discarded what they stated, and that ambiguity is what had me file a false request against hugh. Each refused statement is now named with its reason, and having no clause reads differently from refusing one.\n\nTestRetiredAndStaleClausesDoNotAdmit is replaced rather than deleted: retirement stays pinned as refusing, staleness becomes pinned as admitting-with-notice, and a third test is built from the live workroom's own shape. Mutation-checked by restoring the old condition, which makes that shape refuse as retired and fails both new tests.\n\ngo vet and the full suite pass, and the worktree is clean at this head.","body":{"branch":"request/github-connector-render","commit":"84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3","head":"84ec16239144ef679b6aef811ddf2a75bc5002a3","path":"internal/connector"}}